From: Kristianaaron <25537000+Kristianaaron@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci: tegra: stop the mailbox and padctl IRQs before shutdown powers off

tegra_xusb_shutdown() runtime-resumes the controller (which reloads its
firmware), disables only the xHCI interrupt, calls xhci_shutdown() and then
tegra_xusb_disable(), which turns the XUSB clocks and power off. The
firmware mailbox interrupt and the padctl wake interrupt stay enabled. Their
threaded handlers access XUSB registers, so a mailbox message handled after
tegra_xusb_disable() faults:

  tegra-xusb 70090000.usb: Firmware timestamp: 2023-04-25 07:35:59 UTC
  SError Interrupt on CPU0, code 0x00000000bf000002 -- SError
  CPU: 0 UID: 0 PID: 144 Comm: irq/77-70090000 ...
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Asynchronous SError Interrupt

(IRQ 77 is the controller's mailbox interrupt.) On a Jetson Nano this hit
warm reboots intermittently, which then hung or ended in a panic.

Disable the mailbox interrupt, and the padctl interrupt when the device tree
provides one, together with the xHCI interrupt. disable_irq() also waits for
a handler that is already running. This extends the shutdown callback added
by "usb: xhci: tegra: Add shutdown callback for Tegra XUSB" (2023).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-tegra.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-tegra.c
@@ -2020,6 +2020,14 @@
 
 	pm_runtime_get_sync(&pdev->dev);
 	disable_irq(tegra->xhci_irq);
+	/*
+	 * Also stop the firmware mailbox and padctl wake interrupts: their threads access
+	 * XUSB registers, and tegra_xusb_disable() below turns the controller's clocks and
+	 * power off. A mailbox message handled after that faults (asynchronous SError).
+	 */
+	disable_irq(tegra->mbox_irq);
+	if (tegra->padctl_irq > 0)
+		disable_irq(tegra->padctl_irq);
 	xhci_shutdown(tegra->hcd);
 	tegra_xusb_disable(tegra);
 }
